{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Cross-epic interaction with RP-06 (uneducated-habitual-primate), specifically S1 `dietetic-pompous-boar` \"Compile immutable effective review-policy snapshots\".\n\nS1 creates an immutable repository-bound `CriteriaSnapshot` in `rebar.llm.criteria` that folds effective built-ins + project LLM/DET criteria + routing/posture/applicability into ONE authority, replacing today's \"packaged-only overlay and detector registries\" reads (its stated defect: \"a project disable or RETUNE can be ignored\"). Its file_impact includes new `llm/criteria/{snapshot,overlay}.py` and `.rebar/criteria_routing.json`.\n\nThis calibration edits the PACKAGED `src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json` (flips api-compat/deletion-impact/regression/error-handling to blocking). That packaged routing is exactly what S1 restructures the consumption of.\n\nRelationship = landing-order COORDINATION, not a blocking dependency:\n- S1's golden contract tests pin \"current behavior … allow only the approved corrections.\" If these calibrated blocking thresholds are not present when S1 captures its baseline, S1 will either flag them as an unapproved delta or the new snapshot silently drops the retune.\n- Whichever lands first, the other side must preserve the calibrated thresholds: land these flips before S1's golden capture, OR have S1 include them in its approved baseline.\n\nLinked `relates_to` S1 (dietetic-pompous-boar) to make this visible to whoever executes either side. No relationship to the write-parity siblings (scratchy/topaz/blusterous/churlish/linen) — those touch the write-op adapter subsystem, disjoint from RP-06's review-gate discovery subsystem (no shared files, no behavioral coupling)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787083237416653001,"uuid":"67cb23f0-7777-485e-915c-1483ab3d78bd"}